  "description": "NEKNOK crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P 1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C43 H58 F18 Gd4 N4 O24,4(C1 H4 O1),2.5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.381-3.865 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 84.14-107.59°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C47H79F18Gd4N4O30.5. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
